----------------------------------------------------------------------

CROSS-PLATFORM C++/CMAKE .GITIGNORE

----------------------------------------------------------------------

1. BUILD FOLDER OUTPUT

CMake uses the 'build/' folder for all temporary files and final binaries.

It should NEVER be committed.

build/
bin/
out/
Release/
Debug/

2. CMAKE ARTIFACTS

These files are generated by CMake and are specific to your machine/IDE.

CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt
Makefile
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/

3. VISUAL STUDIO / WINDOWS ARTIFACTS

If you are using VS Code or Visual Studio on Windows, these files track settings.

*.sln               # Visual Studio Solution File (often committed, but safer to ignore)
*.vcxproj           # Visual Studio Project File
*.vcxproj.filters   # Filters for VS solution explorer
*.user
*.pdb               # Program Debug Database
*.ilk               # Incremental Linker File
*.obj               # Object files
*.exe               # Executable binary
*.aps
*.ncb
*.suo
ipch/
.vs/                # Visual Studio's hidden state folder

4. VS CODE (Optional but recommended)

Files that are local VS Code settings

.vscode/

.vscode/settings.json # Optional: If you want to commit shared settings

.vscode/tasks.json    # Optional: If you want to commit shared tasks

5. COMMON LOGS & TEMP FILES

*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~